# Generated evidence, not source - each capability-check script
# (scripts/run-*-capability-check.mjs, scripts/run-*-benchmark.mjs) writes one
# timestamped JSON result file here as committed proof of a real run.
# Reformatting them is pure noise: they are data, never hand-edited, and their
# content is defined entirely by whatever produced them.
benchmarks/results/

# pnpm's own lockfile. Reformatting it (confirmed by running `prettier --write .`
# once and inspecting the diff before reverting) rewrites every single-line
# `resolution: {integrity: ...}`/`engines: {...}` flow mapping onto several
# lines - technically still valid YAML, but a ~1000-line diff on a file no
# human ever hand-edits, that would make every future PR touching a dependency
# noisy and conflict-prone for no benefit. pnpm itself, not prettier, owns this
# file's formatting.
pnpm-lock.yaml
